Subject: [PATCH 09/10] WP-0.7, enforcement (cld-advisor's series 4, patch 9;
 built on 87bfa1f05 with series 3 and the first eight patches of series 4
 applied): AN AMENDMENT TO THE SERIES' THIRD PATCH -- A REVIEW'S ANCHOR MAY BE
 THE HEAD ITS READERS READ, AND IT IS NOT RETYPED. The third patch held the
 last review's anchor to the commit in which its entry landed, which is what
 main's last eight reviews did. Review 79, entered after the patch was sent,
 names the head its readers read: an ancestor of the commit that carries the
 entry, so that what landed between the two is counted for the next review.
 That is the better anchor, and the rule as sent refused it: on main's
 87bfa1f05 the gate that blocks until the review is run read that the anchor
 is typed 0dda7b472 and its entry landed in 84baf38fb, and failed. The fault
 is the seat's: it took a habit of eight reviews for the rule. THE RULE NOW,
 in three parts. One anchor, on a line of its own, and nothing after it names
 another: as sent. The anchor is not later than its entry: it is the commit
 that carries the entry, or an ancestor of it. And the anchor is what it was
 when it first stood: the first commit in which the entry named an anchor is
 read from history, and a later change of that line is refused, to a later
 commit or to an earlier one. So a sentence that names the head still moves
 nothing; an anchor retyped to the entry's own commit, which would take the
 landings in between out of the count, is refused; and a review that lands
 moves the anchor, as before. AND THERE IS A WAY OUT OF A MISTAKE: an anchor
 that names no commit, or a commit later than its entry, never stood, since
 the gate is red on it; putting it right is not a retyping. As the amendment
 was first built it refused that correction too, and nothing main could type
 would have made the gate pass again; the seat found it by reading its own
 rule before sending it. No test of the third patch's lock is taken out or
 renamed; its file keeps its name, with a dated note; one sentence of the gate
 is reworded and still says where the entry landed. What it does not reach, as
 before: a whole entry that is made up and landed as a review is landed. What
 it does not reach, besides: an anchor that stood and was the wrong ancestor
 stays until the next review lands. The lock: four tests added to
 tests/test_the_reviews_anchor_is_the_commit_it_landed_in.py. On the commit
 before, on main's 87bfa1f05, with the lock as this patch leaves it: four fail
 and six pass. The test that reads this repository fails because the gate
 refuses Review 79's own anchor; one because the gate refuses an anchor that
 names the head the review read; one because an anchor retyped after it stood
 passes; and the test of the way out fails at its first step, because the rule
 as sent does not say of a mistyped anchor that it names no commit. On the
 amendment as first built, which was not sent, that test fails where it is
 meant to: the anchor put right is refused as a retyping. Tested against
 planted errors; computed once. 0 of 19.

---
 scripts/gates/gates.py                        | 46 +++++++++-
 ...views_anchor_is_the_commit_it_landed_in.py | 84 ++++++++++++++++++-
 2 files changed, 126 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/scripts/gates/gates.py b/scripts/gates/gates.py
index 4976a898f..d03e23fd9 100644
--- a/scripts/gates/gates.py
+++ b/scripts/gates/gates.py
@@ -3071,12 +3071,52 @@ def review_anchor_problems(text=None):
     landed = out.split()[-1] if rc == 0 and out.split() else None
     if landed is None:
         return [f"cannot verify: the commit in which the entry of Review {n} landed is not in this history"]
-    if not landed.startswith(own_line[0]):
-        return [f"the anchor of Review {n} is typed {own_line[0][:9]}, and its entry landed in {landed[:9]}: the anchor is the commit "
-                "in which the review landed, and it moves only when a review lands"]
+    # AMENDED 2026-11-12 (the series' ninth patch).  As first sent, the anchor had to BE the commit in which the entry landed,
+    # as in main's last eight reviews.  Review 79 names the head its readers read, an ancestor of the commit that carries the
+    # entry, so that what landed between the two is counted for the next review; the rule as sent refused it.  The anchor is
+    # now held to two things: it is not later than its entry, and it is what it was when it first stood.  An anchor that names
+    # no commit, or a later commit, never stood: the gate is red on it, and putting it right is not a retyping.
+    typed = own_line[0]
+    rc, full = _git("rev-parse", "--verify", "--quiet", typed + "^{commit}")
+    full = full.strip()
+    if rc != 0 or not full:
+        return [f"the anchor of Review {n} is typed {typed[:9]}, which is no commit of this history"]
+    if full != landed and _git("merge-base", "--is-ancestor", full, landed)[0] != 0:
+        return [f"the anchor of Review {n} is typed {typed[:9]}, and its entry landed in {landed[:9]}: an anchor is the head the "
+                "review read or the commit that carries its entry, and never a later one"]
+    first = _anchor_as_first_stood(n, landed)
+    if first is None:
+        return [f"cannot verify: the commit in which the anchor of Review {n} first stood is not in this history"]
+    if first[1] != full:
+        return [f"the anchor of Review {n} was typed {first[0][:9]} when it first stood, and is typed {typed[:9]} now: an anchor is "
+                "not retyped; it moves only when a review lands"]
     return []
 
 
+def _anchor_as_first_stood(n, landed):
+    """(as typed, the commit it names): the first anchor of Review `n` that STOOD, read along main's own line from the commit
+    in which the entry landed; None where that cannot be read.  An anchor stands where it names a commit that is the
+    entry's own or an ancestor of it.  One that names no commit, or a later commit, never stood: the gate was red on it,
+    and putting it right is not a retyping."""
+    rc, out = _git("rev-list", "--first-parent", "--reverse", "HEAD", "--", REVIEWS)
+    commits = out.split() if rc == 0 else []
+    if landed not in commits:
+        return None
+    for c in commits[commits.index(landed):]:
+        rc, page = _git("show", f"{c}:{REVIEWS}")
+        if rc != 0:
+            return None
+        at = [m.start() for m in re.finditer(r"^# Review %d " % n, page, re.M)]
+        if not at:
+            continue
+        for typed in re.findall(r"^\*\*anchor-commit: `([0-9a-f]{7,40})`\*\*[ \t]*$", page[at[-1]:], re.M)[:1]:
+            rc, full = _git("rev-parse", "--verify", "--quiet", typed + "^{commit}")
+            full = full.strip()
+            if rc == 0 and full and (full == landed or _git("merge-base", "--is-ancestor", full, landed)[0] == 0):
+                return typed, full
+    return None
+
+
 def gate_review_fires(_merges=None):
